				}
			},
			{
				"box": {
					"code": "/*\r\n * sr.blur.v.genjit\r\n *\r\n * Vertical pass of separable Gaussian blur\r\n * Part of SevenRad Max 8 Effects\r\n *\r\n * Parameters:\r\n *   sigma (float 0.0-50.0): Gaussian standard deviation\r\n *\r\n * Usage:\r\n *   Chain with sr.blur.h for full 2D Gaussian blur:\r\n *   [jit.gl.pix @gen sr.blur.h] -> [jit.gl.pix @gen sr.blur.v]\r\n *\r\n * Algorithm:\r\n *   - Calculates blur radius as 3 * sigma (covers 99.7% of Gaussian)\r\n *   - Samples vertically with Gaussian weights\r\n *   - Normalizes by sum of weights to preserve brightness\r\n *\r\n * Note:\r\n *   Both passes must use the same sigma parameter for correct results.\r\n *   Separable implementation is O(n) instead of O(n^2) for large sigma.\r\n *\r\n * Source: src/sevenrad_stills/operations/blur_gaussian_taichi.py\r\n */\r\n\r\n\r\n// Calculate blur radius (3 sigma covers 99.7% of distribution)\r\nradius = int(ceil(sigma * 3));\r\n\r\n// Accumulator for weighted color sum\r\nsum = vec(0, 0, 0, 0);\r\nweight_sum = 0;\r\n\r\n// Sample along vertical axis\r\nfor (i = -radius; i <= radius; i += 1) {\r\n    // Gaussian weight function: exp(-x^2 / (2*sigma^2))\r\n    weight = exp(-(i * i) / (2 * sigma * sigma + 0.0001));\r\n\r\n    // Vertical offset in normalized coordinates\r\n    offset = vec(0, float(i) / dim.y);\r\n\r\n    // Accumulate weighted sample\r\n    sum += sample(in1, norm + offset) * weight;\r\n    weight_sum += weight;\r\n}\r\n\r\n// Normalize by total weight to preserve brightness\r\nout1 = sum / max(weight_sum, 0.0001);",
					"fontname": "Arial",
					"fontsize": 12.0,
